From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PonWrt Maintainers <ponwrt@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93: reject zero-length final hash descriptors

The EIP93 reports a ZERO_LENGTH processing error for zero-byte descriptors.
A valid non-empty hash request retains one complete tail block for final()
while a genuinely empty non-HMAC digest is handled in software. Reject an
inconsistent zero-length final state before mapping or publishing a descriptor.

---
--- a/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-hash.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-hash.c
@@ -570,9 +570,11 @@
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-	/* A zero-length final segment is valid after prior hash state. */
-	/* Map the fixed tail buffer; the descriptor length remains data_used. */
-
+	/* EIP93 reports ZERO_LENGTH for a zero-byte descriptor. */
+	if (final && !stage.data_used) {
+		eip93_hash_stage_discard(&stage, eip93->dev);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
 
 	/* A partial update has no hardware transaction to submit yet. */
 	if (!final && !stage.nblocks) {
